The '''throne room''' of the [[Monarch of Naboo|Naboo]] [[Monarchy|monarchs]] was located in the heart of the [[Theed Royal Palace|Royal Palace]] of [[Theed]].<ref name="The Phantom Menace" /> On the request of [[Royal Naboo Security Forces]] [[Captain]] [[Quarsh Panaka]], the [[Naboo Royal Handmaidens|handmaiden]] [[Eirtaé]] installed a compartment within the [[throne]], only accessible by the [[Monarch of Naboo|queen]] that concealed two small [[blaster pistol]]s, allowing the newly appointed [[Queen]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] to be prepared for the worst when hosting foreign dignitaries.<ref name="Queen's Peril">''[[Queen's Peril]]''</ref>

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The throne room, as with the rest of the Palace's interior, was filmed on location inside [[Wikipedia:Italy|Italy's]] [[Wikipedia:Royal Palace of Caserta|Royal Palace of Caserta]] for both [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']] and its sequel [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']]. The Queen's desk and other furniture were set dressing for the films and not part of the real palace.<ref name="Galactic Backpacking 2">{{SW|url=news/galactic-backpacking-part-2-visiting-real-world-naboo|text=Galactic Backpacking, Part 2: Visiting Real-World Naboo|nolive=1}}</ref>

